From: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v3dv: report subsampled plane extents for single-plane views

The common image view initializer retains the full multi-planar image extent.
V3DV texture descriptors use the selected plane dimensions, but imageSize and
textureSize uniforms use the unadjusted view extent. A chroma view of NV12
therefore reports luma dimensions and normalized-coordinate scaling repeats
only the upper-left portion of the chroma plane.

Use the selected plane's mip dimensions for single-plane YCbCr views, while
leaving combined YCbCr views and non-planar images unchanged.

Signed-off-by: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>

--- a/src/broadcom/vulkan/v3dv_image.c
+++ b/src/broadcom/vulkan/v3dv_image.c
@@ -772,6 +772,17 @@
    /* At this point we should have at least one plane */
    assert(iview->plane_count > 0);
 
+   /* The common view extent describes the full image. A single-plane view
+    * of a subsampled YCbCr image must instead report that plane's extent to
+    * imageSize/textureSize, matching its texture descriptor dimensions. */
+   if ((image->vk.aspects & any_plane_aspect) && iview->plane_count == 1) {
+      const uint8_t plane = iview->planes[0].image_plane;
+      iview->vk.extent.width = u_minify(image->planes[plane].width,
+                                      iview->vk.base_mip_level);
+      iview->vk.extent.height = u_minify(image->planes[plane].height,
+                                       iview->vk.base_mip_level);
+   }
+
    const VkImageSubresourceRange *range = &pCreateInfo->subresourceRange;
 
